      "message": "Right. That\u0027s one of the two purposes of the shims: simplify production code by abstracting away the differences between releases. It should be very simple, just:\n\npackage com.android.networkstack.apishim.api30;\n\n...\n\npublic class ConnectivityManagerShimImpl\n        extends com.android.networkstack.apishim.api29.ConnectivityManagerShimImpl {\n\n...\n\n    @Override\n    public void registerSystemDefaultNetworkCallback(@NonNull NetworkCallback networkCallback,\n            @NonNull Handler handler) {\n        final NetworkRequest request \u003d new NetworkRequest.Builder()\n                .clearCapabilities()\n                .addCapability(NetworkCapabilities.NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_RESTRICTED)\n                .addCapability(NetworkCapabilities.NET_CAPABILITY_TRUSTED)\n                .addCapability(NetworkCapabilities.NET_CAPABILITY_NOT_VPN)\n                .addCapability(NetworkCapabilities.NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET)\n                .build();\n        mCm.requestNetwork(request, networkCallback, handler);\n    }\n}",
